      "description": "Fine Arts on display at the first Queensland Intercolonial Exhibition, Brisbane, 1876\nThe walls of the main exhibition building are covered with paintings and photographs entered under the 'Fine Arts' section of the exhibition. The glass case on the left contains millinery of the kind that earned a first-class certificate for exhibitor Madame Harrie of Brisbane. The case surmounted by the stuffed ram at the right of the picture was part of the display of Messrs John Vicars and Company of Sydney. This company produced fine tweed cloth and shawls hanging from the corners of their show-case, are examples of the work which was produced during the exhibiton on their Jacquard power loom. (Description supplied with photograph.).",
